    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Permethrin 5% cream from the neck down, washed off after 8 to 14 hours; repeat in 7 days. In infants and young children also the head and neck, avoiding the eyes and mouth"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Spinosad 0.9% suspension (age 4 and older) from the neck down, including the soles; leave on 6 hours; repeat in 1 week"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Precipitated sulfur 6 to 10% in petrolatum: an alternative typically reserved for infants"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Lindane: MSD says it is no longer recommended (neurotoxic); CDC keeps it only for patients who can't tolerate, or have failed, recommended therapy. Aplastic anemia has also been reported"
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
